### REST Client examples for World Cup Predictor API

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@sessionCookie = JSESSIONID=PASTE_VALID_SESSION_COOKIE_HERE
@predictionId = 1

### 1) Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### 2) Start OAuth2 login and capture session cookie
# copy and past into a browser to complete the login flow 
# and capture the JSESSIONID cookie value for subsequent requests.
# This request redirects to Google OAuth2 and creates a JSESSIONID cookie for the local app.
# In the REST client, inspect the response headers for Set-Cookie and copy the JSESSIONID value.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login?redirect_uri=http://localhost:4200/login&redirectUrl=http://localhost:4200/login&returnUrl=http://localhost:4200/login
Accept: application/json

### 3) Verify the authenticated session
# Paste the JSESSIONID cookie value from the /api/auth/login response into the @sessionCookie variable above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### 4) Get current authenticated user
# Requires a valid session cookie.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### 5) Get predictable match catalog for dropdowns
# Returns a top-level array of match objects.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/matches
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### 6) Create a new prediction
# Requires a valid session cookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/predictions
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

{
  "homeTeam": "Uzbekistan",
  "awayTeam": "Colombia",
  "matchStage": "Group Stage",
  "venue": "",
  "matchDate": ""
}

### 7) Logout (primary frontend contract)
# Idempotent: returns 200 even if no active session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### 8) Logout via GET for manual browser testing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}


### 9) Validate session after logout (expect unauthenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}


### 10) Example unauthenticated error shape (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/matches
Accept: application/json

### Example 401 body
# {
#   "error": {
#     "code": "UNAUTHENTICATED",
#     "message": "Authentication required.",
#     "details": []
#   },
#   "timestamp": "2026-07-13T18:25:43Z",
#   "path": "/api/matches"
# }
